            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to achieve, then the Kannada for to gain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ನೇಮಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನೇಮಿಸು — nēmisu — \"to appoint; to hire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಂಪನಿ ಹತ್ತು ಹೊಸ ನೌಕರರನ್ನು ನೇಮಿಸಿತು. kampani hattu hosa naukararannu nēmisitu. The company hired ten new employees."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ನೇಮಿಸಿದೆ, nēmiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The one appointed takes -ಅನ್ನು. ನೇಮಕ is an appointment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನೇಮಿಸು (nēmisu) is built on nēma, \"a fixed rule or arrangement\", a Kannada form of Sanskrit niyama, \"restraint, fixed law\" (CDIAL 7250), with the verb ending -isu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
